    "promptNode-1683813691363_0.json": {
      "Return only a comma-separated list of named entities that appear in the following text: \"The **chainsaw was invented by several people in stages**, but the earliest version is usually credited to **two Scottish doctors, John Aitken and James Jeffray**, in the **late 1700s**. They developed an early **bone-cutting chain saw** for medical use, especially in childbirth operations.\n\nThe **modern portable chainsaw** used for cutting wood is more directly associated with **Andreas Stihl**, who built an electric chainsaw in **1926** and a gasoline-powered one in **1929**. Later, **Emil Lerp** also helped advance the design of the gas-powered chainsaw.\n\nSo, in short:\n- **Early chainsaw concept:** John Aitken and James Jeffray\n- **Modern chainsaw:** Andreas Stihl\"": [
        {
          "prompt": 84,
          "uid": "383eba72-7f36-4541-97a0-b6d5a962665f",
