      ],
      "Return only a comma-separated list of named entities that appear in the following text: \"The chainsaw was invented by **Bernhard Heine**, a German orthopedic surgeon, in **1830**.\n\nHe called it the **osteotome**, and it was originally designed for **cutting bone during surgery**, not for cutting trees. The modern chainsaw used in forestry came much later and evolved from that early design.\"": [
        {
          "prompt": 88,
          "uid": "ce5f774b-5fa1-4a6c-aa96-e9232d381868",
