            "LLM_0": 87,
            "LLM_1": "GPT-5.4 Mini"
          }
        }
      ],
      "Return only a comma-separated list of named entities that appear in the following text: \"The chainsaw wasn’t invented by just one person in its modern form; it evolved over time.\n\nIf you mean the **first chainsaw-like tool**, it was developed in the **late 18th century** for medical use, specifically by **two Scottish doctors, John Aitken and James Jeffray**. They created an early chain-cutting device to assist in **symphysiotomy** and other surgeries.\n\nIf you mean the **modern portable chainsaw used for cutting wood**, the key development is usually credited to **Andreas Stihl**, who invented one of the first **electric chainsaws** in **1926**, and later **Emil Lerp**, who developed an early **gas-powered chainsaw** in **1929**.\n\nSo the short answer is:\n- **Early chainsaw concept:** John Aitken and James Jeffray\n- **Modern chainsaw development:** Andreas Stihl and Emil Lerp\n\nIf you want, I can also give you a short timeline of chainsaw history.\"": [
        {
          "prompt": 90,
          "uid": "02bcbabe-2c8d-4e3c-9e1b-cc64285e6c10",
          "responses": [
            85
          ],
