            "LLM_0": 87,
            "LLM_1": "GPT-5.4 Mini"
          }
        }
      ],
      "Return only a comma-separated list of named entities that appear in the following text: \"The chainsaw was invented by **Andreas Stihl**, a German engineer who patented the first gasoline-powered chainsaw in **1929**. \n\nHowever, the history is a bit more complex:\n\n- Early chainsaw-like devices existed before Stihl, including a steam-powered saw from the 1830s and an electric chainsaw in the 1920s\n- Stihl's key innovation was creating a practical, gasoline-powered version that was portable and efficient enough for commercial logging\n- He founded his company, STIHL, in 1926, and it remains one of the leading chainsaw manufacturers today\n\nSo while Stihl is credited with inventing the modern chainsaw, it was the result of earlier innovations refined into a practical tool.\"": [
        {
          "prompt": 91,
          "uid": "3a56976f-5e15-4f36-b91b-e746e802dd05",
          "responses": [
            92
          ],
          "llm": "GPT-5.4 Mini",
          "vars": {
