      "Return only a comma-separated list of named entities that appear in the following text: \"Thomas Edison is widely credited with inventing the practical, commercially viable lightbulb in 1879. His version used a carbonized cotton filament in a vacuum bulb and lasted much longer than earlier attempts, making it suitable for widespread use.\n\nHowever, it's worth noting that Edison wasn't the first to work on electric lighting. Other inventors, including Joseph Swan in Britain and Humphry Davy earlier on, contributed to the development of electric light technology. But Edison's innovation made the lightbulb practical and accessible, which is why he's most commonly associated with its invention.\"": [
        {
          "prompt": 99,
