      "Return only a comma-separated list of named entities that appear in the following text: \"Thomas Edison is most commonly credited with inventing the practical, commercially viable lightbulb in 1879. He developed a long-lasting incandescent bulb with a carbonized cotton filament that could burn for many hours.\n\nHowever, it's worth noting that Edison wasn't the first to experiment with electric light. Several inventors before him—including Humphry Davy, Warren de la Rue, and Joseph Swan—had created various forms of electric lighting. But Edison's key achievement was making a bulb that was both durable and practical for everyday use, along with developing the electrical infrastructure to support it.\"": [
        {
          "prompt": 105,
