      "Return only a comma-separated list of named entities that appear in the following text: \"The vacuum cleaner wasn’t invented by just one person in a single step—it evolved over time.\n\nA commonly credited early inventor is **Hubert Cecil Booth**, who patented one of the first practical powered vacuum cleaners in **1901** in the UK.\n\nAnother important early inventor was **Daniel Hess**, who patented an earlier carpet sweeper with suction in **1860** in the US.\n\nSo, if you mean the **modern practical vacuum cleaner**, **Hubert Cecil Booth** is often credited.\"": [
