      "Return only a comma-separated list of named entities that appear in the following text: \"# Back-propagation Algorithm\n\nThe back-propagation algorithm was developed by **David Rumelhart, Geoffrey Hinton, and Ronald Williams** in **1986**.\n\nTheir paper, \"Learning representations by back-propagating errors,\" published in *Nature*, became foundational to modern neural networks and deep learning. However, it's worth noting that the mathematical concepts behind back-propagation were explored earlier by others, including Paul Werbos in 1974, but Rumelhart, Hinton, and Williams are credited with popularizing and demonstrating its practical effectiveness for training multi-layer neural networks.\"": [
