      "Return only a comma-separated list of named entities that appear in the following text: \"The backpropagation algorithm is most commonly credited to **Geoffrey Hinton, David Rumelhart, and Ronald Williams** in their influential 1986 paper.\n\nA bit more context:\n- The core idea of training multilayer neural networks with gradients predates that work.\n- Earlier foundational contributions were made by **Paul Werbos**, who described the method in his 1974 dissertation.\n- Similar ideas also appeared in other earlier research, but **Rumelhart, Hinton, and Williams** are the names most often associated with popularizing it in modern machine learning.\n\nSo, the short answer is: **it was invented earlier by Paul Werbos, and later popularized by Rumelhart, Hinton, and Williams.**\"": [
