      "Return only a comma-separated list of named entities that appear in the following text: \"# Coffee Maker History\n\nThere's no single inventor, as the coffee maker evolved over time through multiple contributions:\n\n- **Early designs (1600s-1700s)**: Various simple brewing methods existed, like the ibrik (still used for Turkish coffee)\n\n- **Drip coffee (1908)**: **Melitta Bentz**, a German housewife, invented the paper filter and drip method, which became very popular\n\n- **Percolator (1865)**: **James Mason** patented an early version, though it was refined by others\n\n- **Espresso machine (1901)**: **Desiderio Pavoni** created the first commercial espresso machine based on designs by **Angelo Moriondo**\n\nSo while **Melitta Bentz** is often credited with the modern drip coffee maker, the coffee maker as a concept has multiple inventors depending on which type you're referring to.\"": [
