      "Return only a comma-separated list of named entities that appear in the following text: \"The back-propagation algorithm was developed by several researchers, but it is most famously credited to **David Rumelhart**, **Geoffrey Hinton**, and **Ronald J. Williams**, who published a key paper in 1986 titled *\"Learning representations by back-propagating errors.\"* However, the method's foundations were laid earlier:\n\n- **Paul Werbos** first described back-propagation in his 1974 Ph.D. dissertation and later in a 1982 paper, though it was not widely recognized at the time.\n- **Seppo Linnainmaa** published a related method for automatic differentiation in 1970, which is a core mathematical basis for back-propagation.\n\nSo, while the algorithm has multiple contributors, the 1986 paper by Rumelhart, Hinton, and Williams popularized it and demonstrated its practical use in neural networks.\"": [
